From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:46:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] GUI: item meshes share one depth clear per frame

drawItemStack cleared the depth buffer before every item it draws as a
mesh (a node without an inventory image). On tiled GPUs a clear that
follows a draw ends the render pass: Mesa's lima submits the frame so
far and reloads it (lima_clear flushes the job when draws are pending).
An inventory page full of blocks drew one whole frame per block and ran
at about 5 FPS on a Mali-400, and the HUD hotbar paid the same for each
block in it.

Each mesh now gets a slice of the depth range of its own, nearer than
the ones drawn before it, so meshes keep their drawing order without a
clear; only the first mesh after a reset clears, as the world's depth is
still there. The reset runs where a frame's 2D drawing starts (the HUD,
the main menu, the menu scenes) and after a model[] scene, which uses
the depth buffer the usual way. After 256 slices it clears again.

The view matrix maps z from -1 to 3 onto 0 to 4/101; the projection's z
row now maps that onto the slice instead of the whole range.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

